\title{IonFamilies: isotope and adduct annotation of LC-MS feature groups}
\description{
One compound gives several LC-MS features: its quasi-molecular ion, other
adducts, in-source fragments, and the isotopes of all of these. This
package annotates that \emph{ion family} within groups of features, typically
the groups made with \code{\link[MsFeatures:groupFeatures]{MsFeatures::groupFeatures()}} on an
\link[xcms:XcmsExperiment]{xcms::XcmsExperiment}.
}
\details{
The workflow has two steps:
\enumerate{
\item \code{\link[=annotateIsotopes]{annotateIsotopes()}} with an \code{\link[=IsotopologueParam]{IsotopologueParam()}} finds isotope
patterns with \code{\link[MetaboCoreUtils:isotopologues]{MetaboCoreUtils::isotopologues()}} and labels them in
CAMERA syntax (\verb{[3][M]+}, \verb{[3][M+1]+}).
\item \code{\link[=annotateAdducts]{annotateAdducts()}} with an \code{\link[=AdductVoteParam]{AdductVoteParam()}} finds adducts and
fragments by neutral-mass voting with a rule list
(\code{\link[=defaultAdductRules]{defaultAdductRules()}}). All supported hypotheses are kept and ranked
(\code{\link[=adductHints]{adductHints()}}); the best \code{nBest} are written as text
(\code{\link[=formatAdducts]{formatAdducts()}}).
}

Annotations are \emph{hints}: they suggest what to check, they do not identify
a compound.
}
